REM BASICA interpreter oracle: run the program directly (no compile step).
REM The oracle toolchain is mounted as D:; the current drive is C: (the test
REM directory). T.BAS writes RESULT.TXT itself and ends with SYSTEM, returning
REM to DOS so the harness can finish.
REM
REM Genuine IBM BASICA.COM is only a launcher for the machine's IBM ROM BASIC, so
REM it cannot run on a clone / under DOSBox. GW-BASIC is IBM BASICA plus Cassette
REM BASIC in one self-contained interpreter (language-identical), so it is the
REM runnable BASICA oracle here.
D:\GWBASIC.EXE T.BAS
